<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-SCA '96 PROFIT SEEN 39 PCT DOWN.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-SCA '96 PROFIT SEEN 39 PCT DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group SCA</p>
<p>(Svenska Cellulosa AB) is expected to report a lower profit</p>
<p>after financial items of 3.52 billion crowns for 1996 compared</p>
<p>to 5.73 billion in 1995, a Reuter poll of 13 analysts showed on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>Forecasts varied between 3.30 billion and 3.73 billion</p>
<p>crowns. The average was 39 percent lower than profits a year</p>
<p>ago.</p>
<p>Profit per share was expected to slip back to 10.60 crowns</p>
<p>from 17.55 crowns in 1995.</p>
<p>SCA's board was expected to announce a dividend of around</p>
<p>the same level as last year. The average of forecasts was for a</p>
<p>dividend of 4.70 crowns compared to 4.75 crowns in 1995.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Aragon,</p>
<p>Carnegie, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Enskilda, Fiba, Fischer,</p>
<p>James Capel, Kleinwort Benson, Paribas, Penser, Salomon</p>
<p>Brothers, Swedbank, and Ohman.</p>
<p>SCA will release its earnings reports on January 30.</p>
<p> (MLN SKR)				 AVG     RANGE</p>
<p> Profit after fin items 1996	3,520  3,300-3,731</p>
<p> Profit after fin items 1997	3,670  2,393-5,054</p>
<p> Profit after fin items 1998	4,280  8,200-6,249</p>
<p> Profit per share, crowns	  10.60   9.50-11.80</p>
<p> Dividend, crowns		     4.70   4.00-5.30</p>
